---
/**
 * The pointer, redrawn as the terminal's own caret: a phosphor block that follows
 * the mouse and inverts whatever it covers — `mix-blend-mode: exclusion` turns
 * green on green black, which is what a real block cursor does to the glyph under
 * it. It blinks while still, as a caret waiting for input does, and holds solid
 * while it moves.
 *
 * It is only armed for a fine pointer, and the native pointer is only hidden once
 * the script has taken over, so a touch screen or a failed script keeps its own
 * cursor. See `scripts/cursor.ts`.
 */
---

<div data-caret aria-hidden="true" class="cursor"></div>

<style>
  .cursor {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 1000;
    width: 1ch;
    height: 1.2em;
    background-color: var(--color-green-900);
    mix-blend-mode: exclusion;
    pointer-events: none;
    visibility: hidden;
    transform: translate3d(-100px, -100px, 0);
    animation: caret 1.06s steps(1, end) infinite;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  .cursor[data-visible] {
    visibility: visible;
  }
  /* Moving, so it is being "typed": solid, the way a caret is while you type. */
  .cursor[data-typing] {
    animation: none;
  }

  @keyframes caret {
    0%,
    50% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
    50.01%,
    100% {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .cursor {
      animation: none;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import '@/scripts/cursor'
</script>
